#: ../../../shared/github/MISSION.md:1
msgid "Mission of the ByByte DIY Project"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../shared/github/MISSION.md:3
msgid ""
"Modern life is impossible to imagine without technology. Yet quality "
"technical education often remains expensive, difficult to understand, or "
"disconnected from real-world practice. Many people who want to learn "
"robotics, electronics, and programming on their own face scattered "
"learning materials, a steep entry barrier, and a lack of guidance or "
"support. As a result, motivation fades quickly, and learning turns into "
"an endless search for random solutions instead of a structured path "
"toward real skills."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../shared/github/MISSION.md:5
msgid ""
"The “ByByte DIY” project was created to make modern STEM education open, "
"understandable, and accessible to everyone. We develop open-source "
"robotics platforms, practical learning materials, and structured courses "
"that help children, teenagers, students, educators, and technology "
"enthusiasts learn through hands-on experience, experimentation, and "
"building real projects."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../shared/github/MISSION.md:7
msgid ""
"We believe that the best way to learn is by creating. Building robots, "
"writing code, experimenting, and solving real problems help develop true "
"engineering thinking, creativity, and confidence. DIY culture encourages "
"curiosity, freedom to experiment, and the ability to modify, improve, and"
" invent new things. The open nature of the project allows anyone not only"
" to learn, but also to share their own ideas and improvements with the "
"community."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../shared/github/MISSION.md:9
msgid ""
"All ByByte DIY platforms and educational materials are developed around "
"the principles of openness and collaborative growth. Anyone can build "
"their own project, follow the learning path, adapt materials for their "
"own needs, or contribute to the community. We strive to create an "
"environment where people are not left alone with technical challenges, "
"but instead learn, explore, and grow together."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../shared/github/MISSION.md:11
msgid ""
"Our mission is to help the next generation move from consuming technology"
" to creating it. We envision a future where children and adults are not "
"intimidated by complex technologies, but understand them, work with them "
"confidently, and use their knowledge to create, innovate, and improve the"
" world around them."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../shared/github/MISSION.md:13
msgid ""
"We aim to inspire and grow a new generation of creators, engineers, and "
"inventors — people who do not simply use technology, but actively shape "
"the future with their own ideas and hands."
msgstr ""

